{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"completion_prefetch_manifest":[{"mode":"skeleton","path":"tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py"},{"mode":"full","path":"referencing-commit e93b4f163962627ca17003998c933afa930038d9"}],"criteria":[{"citation":{"description":"A reference-transaction hook forces the CAS race in the `preparing` state. The real fetch must then fail with a signature that `is_ref_cas_mismatch` recognises. The docstring at 415-421 states the root cause: a loaded host serializes the uncoordinated fetches.","kind":"file","line_end":445,"line_start":391,"path":"tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py"},"criterion":"Root cause confirmed with a deterministic reproduction (for example the race forced, or the control made independent of scheduling).","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"The positive control is a single forced-race fetch with no threads, barrier or retry cap, so its verdict does not depend on thread overlap. The coordination half is now its own test, `test_coordination_prevents_the_cas_race`, which asserts 0 mismatches over 8 rounds. That assertion holds because the lock serializes the fetches, so it can only fail if the lock is broken.","kind":"file","line_end":480,"line_start":414,"path":"tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py"},"criterion":"The test's verdict no longer depends on host load.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"The scheduling-dependent assertion 'expected the uncoordinated parallel fetches to race' is gone. The control now forces the race through the hook. It still fails if the hook is a no-op, because the fetch then succeeds and `is_ref_cas_mismatch` returns false. The only skip is for git older than 2.48, which is not load-related. Commit e93b4f1 is the referencing commit and touches only this test file.","kind":"file","line_end":445,"line_start":414,"path":"tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py"},"criterion":"Bug is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_basis":"unpinned_completion_inputs","material_fingerprint":"018cf19a74e17a3e","metrics":{"alias_index_build_ms":2523,"commits_inspected":3711,"descendant_ids":0,"descendant_scope_ms":8982,"det_ms":12331.2,"diff_validation_ms":67,"distinct_references":3219,"git_history_read_ms":122,"landing_check_ms":2773,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":17548.8,"material_policy_ms":0,"pre_verifier_total_ms":28269,"referencing_commits_found":1,"requests":3,"structural_scan_ms":9287,"ticket_ref_resolution_ms":56,"tool_calls":2,"total_ms":29976.2,"verifier_annotation_ms":73315,"verifier_attempt_count":1,"verifier_attempt_setup_ms":1,"verifier_attempts_ms":338486,"verifier_between_attempts_ms":0,"verifier_build_drift_ms":198,"verifier_call_ms":338489,"verifier_code_snapshot_ms":138,"verifier_completion_agent_ms":17548,"verifier_dispatch_finalization_ms":0,"verifier_dispatch_ms":30573,"verifier_dispatch_setup_ms":597,"verifier_handle_apply_ms":0,"verifier_handle_defaults_ms":0,"verifier_handle_resolution_ms":218124,"verifier_inner_setup_ms":16466,"verifier_no_llm_passthrough_ms":0,"verifier_precheck_context_ms":12322,"verifier_resume_config_ms":0,"verifier_resume_count":0,"verifier_reusable_lookup_ms":2,"verifier_snapshot_enter_ms":0,"verifier_snapshot_exit_ms":0,"verifier_snapshot_gc_ms":7,"verifier_ticket_snapshot_ms":217779,"verifier_unclassified_workflow_steps_ms":0,"verifier_verdict_reconcile_ms":9,"verifier_workflow_ms":29976,"verifier_workflow_residual_ms":97,"verifier_workflow_step_count":7,"verifier_wrapper_finalization_ms":0,"verifier_wrapper_setup_ms":0,"verifier_wrapper_total